---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/martial-arts.css';

const title = 'Vo Lam — Original Vietnam Kung Fu | Ted Johnson Works';
const description = 'A developing Ted Johnson Works book project about Vo Lam, Original Vietnam Kung Fu, and practical martial-arts lessons that can complement another training system.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="site-shell nav">
      <a class="brand" href="/">TED JOHNSON <span>WORKS</span></a>
      <nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="/">Works</a>
        <a href="/start">Start Here</a>
        <a href="/photography">Life in Pictures</a>
        <a href="/picks">Ted’s Picks</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="martial-hero">
      <div class="site-shell">
        <div class="martial-hero-panel">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">MARTIAL ARTS · BOOK ON THE RADAR</p>
            <h1>Vo Lam — Original Vietnam Kung Fu</h1>
            <p class="martial-dek">Not an expert’s encyclopedia. A regular practitioner’s book about unusually useful fighting lessons he was fortunate enough to receive — and how some of those ideas can complement the martial art a reader is already studying.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="martial-mark" aria-label="Vo Lam development mark"><span>VÕ LÂM</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="martial-section">
      <div class="site-shell">
        <div class="martial-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">WORKING POSITION</p>
          <h2>Learn alongside the martial art you already train.</h2>
          <p>The concept does not require a reader to abandon their current system, memorize every Vo Lam form, or become a weapons specialist. It focuses on selected practical lessons that can sit beside the stance, kicking, blocking, movement, timing, and controlled technique work they are already learning.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="vo-lam-grid">
          <article class="vo-lam-card">
            <div class="vo-lam-copy">
              <p class="eyebrow">ARCHIVE IMAGE PLACEHOLDER</p>
              <h3>Vo Lam history</h3>
              <p>Reserved for the real Vo Lam photographs from Ted’s archive. I did not find a confidently identifiable Vo Lam image in the current USE.zip or Library search, so no substitute or AI image is being passed off as history.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="vo-lam-card">
            <div class="vo-lam-copy">
              <p class="eyebrow">NEXT ORIGINAL PHOTOS</p>
              <h3>The iron rings</h3>
              <p>Ted still has his original iron rings. New photographs of those rings can become the strongest visual anchor for this section when they are submitted.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <p class="placeholder-note"><strong>K.I.S.:</strong> keep the book useful and selective. The deeper Vo Lam curriculum can remain context; the book can concentrate on practical principles and selected technique families rather than trying to reproduce an entire system.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="site-shell">
        <article class="book-panel">
          <p class="eyebrow">WORKING SUBTITLE</p>
          <h2>Learn Alongside the Martial Art You’re Already Training</h2>
          <p>The premise is strong because the reader is already learning stance, movement, kicks, blocks, distance, timing, and control. Vo Lam can add another lens instead of asking them to start over.</p>
          <p><strong>Content radar:</strong> the traditional set of seventy-two techniques, elbow-strike material, practical applications, surviving equipment, personal memories, and enough historical context to explain where the lessons came from. Specific technique instruction should be presented as controlled martial-arts training and safety-focused practice, not as injury optimization.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="site-shell footer-row">
      <p>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Ted Johnson Works. Martial-arts book project in development.</p>
      <div class="footer-links">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="/photography">Life in Pictures</a>
        <a href="#main">Back to top</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>
